  "seoTitle": "Illegal Gold Mine in Bogor Incident Update",
  "metaDescription": "Search and rescue operations continue in the Pongkor area of Bogor after 13 miners were confirmed dead at an illegal gold mine, with 13 others still missing.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Search and rescue teams have recovered 13 bodies from an illegal gold mining site located in the Ciguha area of Pongkor, Nanggung, Bogor.",
    "Authorities confirm that 13 additional miners remain trapped or missing, while rescue efforts persist despite facing significant operational challenges.",
    "Local police have launched a criminal investigation into the illegal mining activity occurring within the concessions of PT Antam Tbk."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A rescue operation is underway in the Pongkor region of Nanggung, Bogor, following a collapse at an unauthorized gold mining site. Reports confirm that 13 individuals were recovered dead from the tunnels, and search teams are currently working to locate another 13 people who remain trapped or missing. The incident occurred at a facility situated within the mining concessions of PT Antam Tbk. In response to the tragedy, law enforcement officials have initiated a criminal investigation to identify the financiers and organizers behind the unauthorized operations. The incident has drawn attention to the widespread issue of illegal mining practices, with some reports suggesting that illegal gold production output in Indonesia may exceed that of registered legal entities. Search efforts continue, though teams have cited various difficulties hindering the extraction and recovery process.",
